- **Defensive Detections**: 8 detection rule(s)
- **Mitigations**: 8 mitigation control(s)
- **Interactive Lab**: Available for `windows` (Windows Server 2022 Sandbox)
', 'All findings are corroborated against authoritative sources (MITRE ATT&CK, NVD, CISA KEV).', 'ok', '[{"lab": {"lab_id": "lab_ransomware_sim", "lab_type": "adversary_emulation", "platform": "windows", "available": true, "objective": "Detect volume shadow copy deletion and simulate safe benign file alteration", "difficulty": "Medium", "launchable": true, "network_mode": "air-gapped", "technique_id": "T1486", "session_steps": ["Open PowerShell in Admin mode", "Inspect benign target files in C:\\TestShare", "Run benign encryption simulator", "Analyze Sysmon event logs in Event Viewer"], "technique_name": "Ransomware Encryption & Shadow Copy Defense", "safety_boundary": "Zero-network egress, benign canary files only", "validation_source": "Atomic Red Team T1486", "estimated_duration": "20m", "scenario_objective": "Understand ransomware mechanics and write behavioral Sigma rules", "runtime_environment": "Windows Server 2022 Sandbox"}, "rank": 1, "entity": {"id": "T1486", "name": "Data Encrypted for Impact (Ransomware)", "type": "technique", "taxonomy": "Enterprise ATT&CK", "description": "Adversaries may encrypt data on target systems or on large numbers of systems in a network to interrupt availability to system and network resources. Adversaries often leave extortion notes with payment instructions in exchange for decryption keys.", "description_status": "source_supported"}, "summary": "Adversaries use asymmetric/symmetric encryption algorithms (AES, RSA, ChaCha20) to lock user documents, databases, and system backups, rendering them inaccessible without paying extortion ransom.", "evidence": [{"text": "Ransomware strains like LockBit and WannaCry traverse drive mounts and encrypt files matching targeted extensions using AES/RSA.", "ref_id": "T1486", "status": "confirmed", "category": "source", "source_id": null, "source_ref": null, "source_url": "https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1486/", "evidence_id": "ev_t1486_1", "source_name": "CISA / MITRE ATT&CK", "evidence_ref": null, "provenance_type": "standard_corpus"}], "detection": [{"title": "Mass File Rename / Extension Alteration Alert", "description": "Detect rapid file rename events exceeding 50 modifications/sec with entropy > 7.5 indicating cryptographic cipher activity."}, {"title": "Volume Shadow Copy Deletion (Event 4688 / Sysmon 1)", "description": "Monitor execution of vssadmin.exe delete shadows /all /quiet or wmic shadowcopy delete which precedes ransomware execution."}, {"title": "Mass File Rename / Extension Alteration Alert", "description": "Detect rapid file rename events exceeding 50 modifications/sec with entropy > 7.5 indicating cryptographic cipher activity."}, {"title": "Volume Shadow Copy Deletion (Event 4688 / Sysmon 1)", "description": "Monitor execution of vssadmin.exe delete shadows /all /quiet or wmic shadowcopy delete which precedes ransomware execution."}, {"title": "Mass File Rename / Extension Alteration Alert", "description": "Detect rapid file rename events exceeding 50 modifications/sec with entropy > 7.5 indicating cryptographic cipher activity."}, {"title": "Volume Shadow Copy Deletion (Event 4688 / Sysmon 1)", "description": "Monitor execution of vssadmin.exe delete shadows /all /quiet or wmic shadowcopy delete which precedes ransomware execution."}, {"title": "Mass File Rename / Extension Alteration Alert", "description": "Detect rapid file rename events exceeding 50 modifications/sec with entropy > 7.5 indicating cryptographic cipher activity."}, {"title": "Volume Shadow Copy Deletion (Event 4688 / Sysmon 1)", "description": "Monitor execution of vssadmin.exe delete shadows /all /quiet or wmic shadowcopy delete which precedes ransomware execution."}], "mitigation": [{"id": "M1053", "title": "Data Backup & Offline Replication", "description": "Maintain immutable, air-gapped, or write-once-read-many (WORM) backups disconnected from the primary network directory."}, {"id": "M1040", "title": "Behavior Prevention on Storage Systems", "description": "Configure endpoint and network file shares with anti-ransomware canary traps and automated account isolation triggers."}, {"id": "M1053", "title": "Data Backup & Offline Replication", "description": "Maintain immutable, air-gapped, or write-once-read-many (WORM) backups disconnected from the primary network directory."}, {"id": "M1040", "title": "Behavior Prevention on Storage Systems", "description": "Configure endpoint and network file shares with anti-ransomware canary traps and automated account isolation triggers."}, {"id": "M1053", "title": "Data Backup & Offline Replication", "description": "Maintain immutable, air-gapped, or write-once-read-many (WORM) backups disconnected from the primary network directory."}, {"id": "M1040", "title": "Behavior Prevention on Storage Systems", "description": "Configure endpoint and network file shares with anti-ransomware canary traps and automated account isolation triggers."}, {"id": "M1053", "title": "Data Backup & Offline Replication", "description": "Maintain immutable, air-gapped, or write-once-read-many (WORM) backups disconnected from the primary network directory."}, {"id": "M1040", "title": "Behavior Prevention on Storage Systems", "description": "Configure endpoint and network file shares with anti-ransomware canary traps and automated account isolation triggers."}], "attack_chain": [{"steps": ["Inhibit System Recovery via vssadmin", "Traverse local and shared file systems", "Encrypt user files and drop ransom note"], "status": "confirmed", "tactic": "Impact", "description": "Ransomware deployment and encryption sequence", "evidence_ids": ["ev_t1486_1"], "technique_id": "T1486", "lab_available": true, "technique_name": "Data Encrypted for Impact"}], "relationships": [], "missing_evidence": ["Decryption key recovery without payment"]}, {"lab": null, "rank": 2, "entity": {"id": "S0154", "name": "Cobalt Strike (Beacon)", "type": "tool", "taxonomy": "MITRE ATT&CK Software", "description": "Cobalt Strike is a c