## Summary

Persistence via Task Scheduler remains a premier technique across commodity and APT groups due to native OS integration....

## Turn History

### Q: How do attackers establish persistence via scheduled tasks in Windows?

Adversaries frequently leverage the Windows Task Scheduler (MITRE ATT&CK T1053.005) to execute malicious binaries or scripts at system startup or on scheduled recurring intervals. By registering tasks under elevated privileges such as SYSTEM or LocalService via schtasks.exe or Register-ScheduledTask, attackers establish resilient persistence that survives system reboots and administrative session logoffs.

